{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And a new king arose over Egypt, etc.</b> The language of 'arising' we do not find with reference to a king, for it should have said 'and a new king reigned over Egypt' — what is the meaning of 'arose'? And it appears that the language of arising applies to one who rises up against his fellow to do him harm, as it is written (Genesis 4:8) ״וַיָּקָם קַיִן עַל הֶבֶל אָחִיו וַיַּהַרְגֵהוּ״, and it is written (Deuteronomy 22:26) ״כִּי כַּאֲשֶׁר יָקוּם אִישׁ עַל רֵעֵהוּ וּרְצָחוֹ נֶפֶשׁ״. So too this tyrant king — through the devices that he devised to do to Israel against the will of the El, blessed be He, even though he saw that HaShem was with them in that they were fruitful and multiplied beyond the way of the world — nevertheless he sought to outwit Him, blessed be He, and through this he brought it about that HaShem returned their toil upon their own heads, by means of the plagues of wrath and fury that HaShem sent upon them, as it is written (Exodus 10:7) ״הֲטֶרֶם תֵּדַע כִּי אָבְדָה מִצְרָיִם״, and from this it is as though he arose against them to bring upon the Egyptians all those plagues." "And it says <b>'who did not know Joseph'</b> — for he did not know what happened to Joseph, because his brothers exerted themselves with all their might to destroy him and to annul his dreams, and none of their stratagems that they devised availed them, for the will of the El, blessed be He, was with Joseph to exalt him, and the word of our God shall stand forever (Isaiah 40:8). So too Pharaoh said ״פֶּן יִרְבֶּה״ (Exodus 1:10), against the will of the El, blessed be He, who said ״כֵּן יִרְבֶּה״ (Exodus 1:12), and he devised plans against them but did not succeed, just as the brothers of Joseph did not succeed. And in all that he arose to do against Israel, that arising was upon the Egyptians, and upon their scalps did his wrath descend."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:17:42.422409845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}